{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYKrMxoUEBdBvp9pHyP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Within a few days of disclosure, the scope of the Cursor Marketplace incident had changed twice. The first reporting said the Claude Code extension on Open VSX was compromised, and that was later corrected: the incident traces to Cursor's marketplace, and Socket, Microsoft and Cursor found no sign the malicious build reached Open VSX, the Microsoft VS Code Marketplace or the anthropic-ai/claude-code npm package. Cursor's own advisory also widened. It first listed only anthropic.claude-code version 2.1.313 and now names both 2.1.312 and 2.1.313 as affected on Windows and macOS.\n\nThat matters for anyone who checked their machines once, early on. An audit that looked only for 2.1.313, or only at Open VSX installs, would have missed part of the picture. Cursor says at most 5,000 users installed the malicious version, between about 2:27 a.m. and 1:35 p.m. PT on October 29, and Anthropic describes it as live for close to 12 hours.\n\nThe statements from the parties involved also differ in emphasis. Cursor said the malicious version \"was not developed by Anthropic.\" Anthropic said its systems and employee laptops were not compromised and that an actor used their access to Cursor's marketplace to publish a tampered version. The Hacker News noted that the first statement leaves out that the package shipped under Anthropic's real extension ID. Still unanswered is how the attacker obtained that publishing ability and how far their access went.\n\nThe package tried to add an SSH key, set up persistence and send host details, and Cursor says those steps happen even where enabling the SSH service fails for lack of admin rights. So a host that was only exposed briefly may still carry leftovers that uninstalling the extension will not remove. Microsoft's guidance is to remove keys, tunnel identities, scripts and startup entries separately and to rotate credentials."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2156,"cache_read_input_tokens":4205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2156},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e333183c-0259-49fe-aedc-36b6d6a5dc45","uuid":"c6f87d28-e97b-4078-a615-312ee4342ab6","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:22:15.550Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYKr9KLmRjPn5i9D1FG"}
